# Renders.
#
# Both bin/glitchvape and bin/glitchvape-batch default their output here, so
# this fills with megabytes on the first run and with hundreds of megabytes
# after an afternoon of --all-presets. Nothing in it is source: every file is
# reproducible from its seed and the settings that produced it.
#
# Unanchored, so a batch run started from a subdirectory is caught too.
out/

# Source photographs.
#
# The input side of the same coin, and not the program's to distribute.
Pictures/

# Typefaces.
#
# A font belongs in this repository only if it came with permission to hand it
# on. The rule is the one `make check-licenses` and `make dist` apply: a
# release unpacked whole -- LICENSE, README and all -- may be committed; a
# font file dropped in loose may not, because nothing beside it says what its
# terms are.
#
# So everything under assets/fonts/ is ignored by default and the releases
# that are ours to distribute are named back in, one line each. Adding a font
# to the distribution is therefore a deliberate line here plus the unpacked
# licence beside it, and never something that happens by forgetting.
#
# Held back today: VCR OSD Mono and W95FA, both free to use, neither yet
# established as free to redistribute inside somebody else's package. Nothing
# breaks without them -- GlitchVape::Fonts falls through each role's candidate
# list to whatever fontconfig can see, and --check-fonts names the download
# and the directory to put it in. See "Fonts" in the README.
assets/fonts/*
!assets/fonts/DepartureMono-1.500/
!assets/fonts/fusion-pixel-font-12px-monospaced-otf-v2026.08.11/

# Artwork is deliberately NOT ignored: assets/artwork/logo.png is a few
# kilobytes, is this project's own, and the about window needs it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated by the tools this project is checked with

# perltidy leaves a .bak when it is run without the -bext='/' that the
# Makefile-less workflow in the README uses, writes a .ERR beside any file it
# could not parse, and a .LOG when asked for one.
*.bak
*.ERR
*.LOG
*.tdy

# prove --state
.prove

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local tooling and editors

# Claude Code keeps shared settings in .claude/settings.json and personal ones
# -- permission grants, machine-specific paths -- in the .local.json beside
# it. Only the personal half is ignored, so a shared config can still be
# committed if there is ever a reason to.
.claude/settings.local.json

.vscode/
.idea/

*~
*.swp
*.swo

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
